450" :question/math-academy-id "q-42733" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-2\\cdot (-2))+2\\cdot (0\\cdot 0)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+12+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42733/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92053541-63fa-5cca-b3d8-0f4864c31051"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42733"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97410/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "f421beed-3ecf-5c65-ad4e-fe4955afd29e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97410/selection/54e998e2b9613564e4db88fa790dea7921b62f7340b79dc7ba61859b983ac0f6" :answer/id #uuid "75123481-23ce-5398-b68c-1355b8289060" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97410/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" :answer/id #uuid "5ad86efb-3382-5097-9983-807a7c2af578" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97410/selection/a038cf4df09c65d711c1174200281cc22b8be446497e9dc942f4f18d8fa119e2" :answer/id #uuid "1ef57544-e763-58e1-be2a-538c7f4a5d42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97410/selection/d79808b1304c1856f3712e6e226ade34c7caf51f0407b91d3e2447e1f8a4