db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97417" :question/id #uuid "65d60515-7767-5b6f-afb5-20fa2b5f3e11" :question/math-academy-id "q-97417" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=2t-{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2t-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=1,\\,p(0)=0,\\,p(-1)=-3.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(0)p(0)+p(-1)p(-1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(-1)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+0+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97417/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97417"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42726"] :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=1-2t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=1-2t,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=-1,\\,p(2)=-3,\\,p(3)=-5.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42734"] :question/problem "Let $V=C[\\pi ,2\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[\\pi ,2\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{t}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{4}){|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{2\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\pi }{4})-(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =(\\pi +0)-(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we made use of the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡t=\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖f(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-97715/selection/eef0b2dae22f83ad37ffb6972dc152e691bc949b2d9cf82055b70566b56b65c3" :answer/id #uuid "2a176b9b-3ad3-54dc-a5cd-8dcba04bcc49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{56}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97715/selection/0ba6fd3aa8cb0c6737b13b3704564ce2c8ce16db76809dec1eda8534a5292e27" :answer/id #uuid "83109460-cef8-5910-80c3-adc60d429565" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{68}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97715/selection/1e1ae0a1688a75516c21345a9d1557ba3d5d337904e86ece943375dafaf45c97" :answer/id #uuid "780bef2d-2dc6-55eb-b3d3-eaab589560c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{34}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97715/selection/c923d8f98c24389a5a84f11f78907722bee02de9bba5f4e01bb96f765cbf0564" :answer/id #uuid "1f144e6a-a021-58eb-a667-588689647fcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{23}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97715/selection/abd3d2687c1b37a0abd8148877d19bbe512ed06ace01cd25635450d16769eba3" :answer/id #uuid "fd586785-2ba5-562c-93f1-49932febf369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{32}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97715/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc263b3a-4faa-58ce-9317-8fec92f98b04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97715/selection/0ba6fd3aa8cb0c6737b13b3704564ce2c8ce16db76809dec1eda8534a5292e27" :answer-field/choices ["q-97715/selection/eef0b2dae22f83ad37ffb6972dc152e691bc949b2d9cf82055b70566b56b65c3" "q-97715/selection/0ba6fd3aa8cb0c6737b13b3704564ce2c8ce16db76809dec1eda8534a5292e27" "q-97715/selection/1e1ae0a1688a75516c21345a9d1557ba3d5d337904e86ece943375dafaf45c97" "q-97715/selection/c923d8f98c24389a5a84f11f78907722bee02de9bba5f4e01bb96f765cbf0564" "q-97715/selection/abd3d2687c1b37a0abd8148877d19bbe512ed06ace01cd25635450d16769eba3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97715" :question/id #uuid "b1a41dda-d8f9-5690-92f2-1ed2d1f5820d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97715" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,4]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,4],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{4}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=\\sqrt{t}+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\sqrt{t}+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(t+2\\sqrt{t}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{4t\\sqrt{t}}{3}+t)|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =(8+\\frac{32}{3}+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{68}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{68}{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97715/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43921/selection/8f3ef73b7999870c68e02c54e14bf59d32e0c05408243c9952a057bf19f6acf5" :answer/id #uuid "d7f2a67f-8d20-59ca-b6c0-78678601f19a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43921/selection/d65ab5694d946eb620bfc4935477bffe2aca3faa7b67a11968938fabb43d0823" :answer/id #uuid "4dd860b4-a09f-50ad-863b-324c4efc37a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43921/selection/3473306f375fe4cd10d0b0358c1e272dcbb9940574f7b55b9dc2a9035e47f48f" :answer/id #uuid "7f71ce10-a80e-52a2-8473-98f666dd5799" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi +\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43921/selection/2bb248346834586e66e2b9c5633835c3d863fd25b4f81bc0bb31745cd846108b" :answer/id #uuid "3d56d056-3b2b-5686-92dd-f3b930116b54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi +1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43921/selection/7588f01677744ddb693c2eeed655549ef2f2749a671a64c9ba9a6becd838a362" :answer/id #uuid "46866437-8698-5100-b296-08bd1c937daa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi }{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43921/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4be0730-02f0-5964-95e5-fc118bc62c9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43921/selection/8f3ef73b7999870c68e02c54e14bf59d32e0c05408243c9952a057bf19f6acf5" :answer-field/choices ["q-43921/selection/8f3ef73b7999870c68e02c54e14bf59d32e0c05408243c9952a057bf19f6acf5" "q-43921/selection/d65ab5694d946eb620bfc4935477bffe2aca3faa7b67a11968938fabb43d0823" "q-43921/selection/3473306f375fe4cd10d0b0358c1e272dcbb9940574f7b55b9dc2a9035e47f48f" "q-43921/selection/2bb248346834586e66e2b9c5633835c3d863fd25b4f81bc0bb31745cd846108b" "q-43921/selection/7588f01677744ddb693c2eeed655549ef2f2749a671a64c9ba9a6becd838a362"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43921" :question/id #uuid "22161582-39f7-5f14-a415-005aa76ca21c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43921" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\,{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{t}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{4}){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi }{4})-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )}{4}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we made use of the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡t=\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖f(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43921/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43921"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42739/selection/76b12618c5acad81da51767d9b43f0957ad6234e282680ed93ee8d09e1d3a169" :answer/id #uuid "ae09c23e-4833-5bda-9f77-cac16120ff3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(t-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42739/selection/327205574ef247227d2b3c241b95a2d06cf1c8bca4458fccd0f23d78ef89e62e" :answer/id #uuid "c4992185-5ba9-5f5c-a7da-2056e928ccf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(t-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42739/selection/6e7fd1c446cad95195040921ee47ad480cf0f5a866220bee6a38622459b4a1e3" :answer/id #uuid "276ad0ba-d974-5558-81bb-fd06f1d2eb03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}(t-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42739/selection/eaba4da4447c9b33a895d609a3f81feab98b794b9799550831cc4a744e96cb0d" :answer/id #uuid "8738e785-c246-5d60-8da4-b5069be4fdea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42739/selection/23aa4108d61166dc4ce00529ccac7d4a5b9a73d2c777d52a480c69be66e8f0a6" :answer/id #uuid "3dfca35e-08fe-5bb9-95a9-0f5bac654aa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(t-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42739/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "748265bd-ac3c-5cab-8148-81ff2d57a7ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42739/selection/6e7fd1c446cad95195040921ee47ad480cf0f5a866220bee6a38622459b4a1e3" :answer-field/choices ["q-42739/selection/76b12618c5acad81da51767d9b43f0957ad6234e282680ed93ee8d09e1d3a169" "q-42739/selection/327205574ef247227d2b3c241b95a2d06cf1c8bca4458fccd0f23d78ef89e62e" "q-42739/selection/6e7fd1c446cad95195040921ee47ad480cf0f5a866220bee6a38622459b4a1e3" "q-42739/selection/eaba4da4447c9b33a895d609a3f81feab98b794b9799550831cc4a744e96cb0d" "q-42739/selection/23aa4108d61166dc4ce00529ccac7d4a5b9a73d2c777d52a480c69be66e8f0a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42739" :question/id #uuid "2a226526-c78d-5b45-912b-bc1bae613541" :question/math-academy-id "q-42739" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=t-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(t-1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,({t}^{2}-2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $‖f(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{t-1}{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(t-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-42739/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42739"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141174/selection/46369d0563fb55452c30a226c3b1ae5739668a486ccbf3db567d6186c13f11eb" :answer/id #uuid "eacab1e4-8780-58a1-bee7-2ccbc24c1be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141174/selection/6c364c80117dc7b3e2fcf2817d506f3c1e65bff65781cae70706672d45d663a4" :answer/id #uuid "ba99b293-2d2e-5988-9135-d30a447404a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141174/selection/7dba34c1c32c1808f732cbe6df105fa40df03cea15fd85370bc14a46a226d2c0" :answer/id #uuid "70363edc-5c98-5acd-9e0e-020072de6b0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141174/selection/e9dd4b479bbb36eece1ea89d91858306b69463c59189308e277da9ee6991940e" :answer/id #uuid "f3f2b646-d45b-5956-b520-550c26e3cfc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141174/selection/af405a398a1c0a37cffdd3ac2038a9655d0a6833464e7e2c7b39bf15982f5712" :answer/id #uuid "25a72321-510d-5011-bdad-cda79db86fd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141174/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f05ae56-af1f-5e7f-bdaa-ec32824f1103" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141174/selection/e9dd4b479bbb36eece1ea89d91858306b69463c59189308e277da9ee6991940e" :answer-field/choices ["q-141174/selection/46369d0563fb55452c30a226c3b1ae5739668a486ccbf3db567d6186c13f11eb" "q-141174/selection/6c364c80117dc7b3e2fcf2817d506f3c1e65bff65781cae70706672d45d663a4" "q-141174/selection/7dba34c1c32c1808f732cbe6df105fa40df03cea15fd85370bc14a46a226d2c0" "q-141174/selection/e9dd4b479bbb36eece1ea89d91858306b69463c59189308e277da9ee6991940e" "q-141174/selection/af405a398a1c0a37cffdd3ac2038a9655d0a6833464e7e2c7b39bf15982f5712"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141174" :question/id #uuid "18ecc628-846f-52e0-b4d5-bd9869c51840" :question/math-academy-id "q-141174" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \n\nNormalize the  vector  $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨v,v⟩ & =2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4+3+1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $v$, we divide $v$ by its norm $‖v‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{‖v‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141174/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141174"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5908"] :question/problem "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is defined as $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle =  2x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 3x_3 y_3.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/assets/1e710ca7b3b7bea626de36181a30869b0f114a4497843c6b6ea8b8966a91d208.png) under this inner product." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
